@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:rdf-editor-entry-pages a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "Page the RDF editor's top-level resources"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/525> ;
    chg:motivation """Large RDF documents can ask the editor to build thousands of rows before the reader can open a
single resource.""" ;
    chg:substance """An RDF editor with c:entryPageSize renders a window of its named resources (c:entry) in IRI order:
c:entryPageSize of them, from page c:page (1-based, 1 when absent; a page past the end shows none). A maintained view
(c:RdfEditorEntryWindow) holds the window and c:RdfEditorPage derives the page's resources on the editor
(c:rdfPageEntry), so a page change reuses the document graph and replaces only the visible rows. A link jumps only to a
resource of the page; one to a resource of another page opens in place like any other IRI with statements of its own.
Arrows (c:arrows) join rows of the page only. An editor without c:entryPageSize renders and behaves as before. Nothing
in the editor changes the page: the application writes c:page.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Existing documents need no changes. Set c:entryPageSize on the editor to opt in, and update c:page
when the application changes pages; keep the document's c:entry statements in the graph.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Remove c:entryPageSize and c:page from editors. The editor again shows all resources listed in
c:entry, and links jump to any of them.""" ;
    chg:affects c:RdfEditor , c:RdfTerm .
